                     /note="Proteins of this family belong to the Di-heme
                     cytochrome C peroxidase subfamily. They are involved in the
                     bioconversion of oleic acid into oxylipins, a group of
                     hydroxylated fatty acids, in Pseudomonas. First, oleic acid
                     is converted by 10S-dioxygenase into hydroperoxide
                     intermediate (10S)-hydroxy-(8E)-octadecenoic acid
